  "body": "Slice 2b of #4081: the **Laser Profile** operation in the app.\n\n**Stacked on #4270 (slice 1) and #4273 (slice 2a).** The branches of those PRs are in a fork, so this PR targets `main` and its diff includes them. The new work is the two commits after the merge commit `2a3670d48`: `a4cc1cf1f` and `ae360094b`. Merge #4270 and #4273 first. After that, this branch takes `git merge origin/main` and its diff is only slice 2b.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Registry**:\n  - New `OpType::LaserProfile`: stored kind id 49 and digest tag 49, appended.\n  - New `Section::Laser` and `Family::Laser`. The Laser family admits only a laser cutter, and a laser cutter admits only that family.\n  - The ribbon shows the Laser section on a laser cutter only.\n  - The family door refuses laser work elsewhere: \"a Laser Profile operation is laser cutting work; ... - mount a laser cutter first\".\n- **Params**: `LaserOp` has the waterjet's stored shape, with `power` (percent of the source's maximum) in place of the abrasive delay. It reuses the waterjet's lead, side and tab types. The command door checks the power: more than 0, at most 100.\n- **Project file**: `LaserDto` (`\"laser_profile\"`), additive.\n- **Generation**: `operation/laser_op.rs` resolves the heights and the laser head's kerf, then calls `motion::laser::laser_profile` (slice 2a).\n- **Machine check**: `machine::waterjet::check_xy_ops` holds the X/Y gantry checks once. These are the family, the tool kind, rotary moves, feed ceilings and strokes. The waterjet and the laser call it with their own words. The waterjet sentences do not change.\n- **Safety refusals until the laser post exists (slice 3)**:\n  - The verification report says \"<op>: laser posting is unavailable: beam on/off records, power records and pierce dwell records are not implemented\".\n  - The stock sim says \"<op>: laser stock removal is not judged: the stock sim has no laser model\".\n  - The lathe voice refuses the op with its own sentence.\n- **Tools**: the starter catalog gets `LZ-KERF-020` (`laser_tool(0.2)`). The empty-rack refusal names it. `camcraft_app::laser_tools` re-exports the tools module.\n- **UI**:\n  - New `laser_page.rs`: kerf, compensation, direction, open-run side and arcs on Geometry; the three heights; tabs; leads; and on Feeds the cut feed, **Power**, and pierce time. A power out of range is named on the page.\n  - New original glyph `assets/ui/svg/op-laser-profile.svg`: an outlined head, a beam, sparks and the kerf gap. `cargo xtask icons` added only its PNG.\n  - The waterjet page's `tab_fields` is shared.\n- **MCP**: no new tool. `add_operation` and `edit_operation` reach the kind through the registry and the DTO. The `add_operation` description names the laser kind (`crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` and `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`).\n- **Docs**:\n  - New guide page `site/content/guide/operations/operations-laser.md`.\n  - The operations index and `check-and-post/machines.md` name the laser.\n  - Decision: `docs/decisions/4081-laser-op.md`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nA laser cutter mounted, before (slice 1: no section) and after (the LASER group):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4081/before-laser-ribbon.png)\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4081/after-laser-ribbon.png)\n\nThe Laser Profile's Feeds tab (new page):\n\n![feeds](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4081/after-laser-feeds.png)\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/machine/laser_profile.rs` (the `machine` suite, 6 tests):\n  - The family on a laser cutter only.\n  - A holed plate: the hole first, every note in the laser's words, and the laser machine check clean.\n  - The tool doors.\n  - Create, edit, undo and redo, and the power door.\n  - A byte-identical project round trip.\n  - The post and sim refusals by name.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp/laser_profile.rs` (the `mcp` suite): add with tabs, edit the power, undo, redo, refuse 120 %, and generate.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/laser_ribbon.rs` (3): the ribbon on a laser cutter only and the dark cell with its tip on a mill; the own glyph and the leads tab; the Feeds tab with the power row and the named bad power.\n- Updated:\n  - `machine/laser_kind.rs`: a laser cutter now admits only the Laser Profile.\n  - `tool_law::no_orphan_tool_kinds`: only the Laser Profile mounts a laser head.\n  - `tool_gate::the_refusal_names_*`.\n  - `ribbon::family_is_derived_not_forked` and `the_probe_appends_its_id_*`.\n  - `operation::tests::stamp_follows_every_input` (50 kinds).\n  - `lathe_voice_tests` (37 refused kinds).\n  - The catalog asset order (64).\n  - The structural mill-tip test.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 626 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (81 min).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: **not run** (owed before ready, as for #4273).\n- No laser post: posting refuses laser work by name (slice 3).\n- No shipped laser machine file and no machine-mode row: a user loads a `.mch` with `\"kind\": \"laser\"`.\n\nChangelog: Operations: a Laser Profile operation (kerf offset, leads, tabs, power) for laser cutter machines; posting is not available yet.\n\nRefs #4081\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
